  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "read-me",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -230,
      "w": 620,
      "text": "DuelBox \u2014 website and in-game GUI.\n\nThese six screens are drawn in Direction C, The Table: the device is the surface you both sit at, so the split between you is a physical fact rather than a graphic device.\n\nThe other three directions are on the Directions page. If you would rather go another way, say which and I will redraw these in it.",
      "page": "page-1"
    },
    {
      "id": "not-a-clone",
      "x": 700,
      "y": -230,
      "w": 560,
      "text": "Deliberately unlike the reference app: a serif display face instead of a rounded cartoon sans, warm inked surfaces instead of flat primaries, a brass centre rule instead of edge score pills, a category-led browse with search instead of one long scroll, and a dealt hand of cards instead of a node track for the tournament.",
      "page": "page-1"
    },
    {
      "id": "pick-one",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -180,
      "w": 700,
      "text": "Four directions, one axis each. C is recommended and is what the Screens page is drawn in \u2014 but the choice is yours, and the other three are real options, not strawmen. Each names its own risk.",
      "page": "page-2"
    }
  ],
